      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1837, settlers Charles Sheldon and Phil Brewer erected the first log cabins that marked Oconomowoc's early settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.oconomowoc-wi.gov/99/History-of-Oconomowoc",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first passenger train touched Oconomowoc on December 14, 1854, linking the town to Milwaukee via the Milwaukee & Mississippi line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oconomowoc%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Oconomowoc's downtown still showcases 19th‑century architecture, with grand Victorian homes lining the lakeshores.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.oconomowoc-wi.gov/99/History-of-Oconomowoc",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Oconomowoc and Lake Country Museum, located downtown, displays artifacts that chronicle the town's rich history.",
